WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.301
What to carry forward.

2
00:00:01.581 --> 00:00:05.699
Separate capability critiques from impact critiques; they age differently.

3
00:00:05.979 --> 00:00:10.971
Score critics claim by claim, as you scored the lab leaders, and expect “partly right.

4
00:00:11.251 --> 00:00:25.779
” Use the critics’ objections as a design checklist: reliability (validate everything), planning and compounding error (checkpoints, verification, recovery), and diffusion (organizational change is the bottleneck, not the model).

5
00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:38.048
And notice that the most careful voices on both sides, METR, the International AI Safety Report, Narayanan and Kapoor’s updates, all revise their views in public when evidence arrives.

6
00:00:38.328 --> 00:00:41.315
That habit, more than any forecast, is what to emulate.

7
00:00:41.595 --> 00:00:46.928
Next lesson turns to the evidence that most directly concerns your career: AI and work.
